          <h2>Questions members ask</h2>
          <h3>Does Sun Life cover physiotherapy?</h3>
          <p>Many Sun Life group plans include physiotherapy under paramedical services, with an annual maximum and often a limit on the amount paid per visit. Your own plan decides the amounts, and you can confirm them in the app under your coverage details before your first visit.</p>
          <h3>Do I need a referral to claim massage therapy?</h3>
          <p>Many plans let you book a registered massage therapist directly, with no referral at all. Some plans ask for a note from a physician before they pay massage therapy or psychology claims, so check your plan booklet or the app before you book.</p>
          <h3>Can my clinic bill Sun Life directly?</h3>
          <p>Some can. A clinic set up with Sun Life can submit the claim at your appointment, and you pay only the part your plan leaves behind. Ask when you book, and have your plan and member numbers ready in the app.</p>
          <h3>What if my claim is larger than my remaining balance?</h3>
          <p>The claim pays up to the balance left under that category. If your plan includes a Health Spending Account, you can often claim the rest against the account in the same app, when the expense is eligible.</p>

          <h2>Find care that fits your Sun Life plan</h2>
          <p>Start with the treatment, then check the claim. Browse the <a href="/#directory">WellFinder directory</a> to compare clinics for physiotherapy, massage therapy, naturopathy and more across Canada, and open pages such as <a href="/clinics-pelvic-floor-physiotherapy">pelvic floor physiotherapy clinics</a> and <a href="/pilates">clinical Pilates clinics</a> to see providers near you. Before you book, confirm your balance in the my Sun Life app and ask the clinic how the visit will appear on your receipt.</p>
          <p>WellFinder is an independent directory and is not affiliated with Sun Life. This guide explains common features of Sun Life group plans in Canada. Your employer plan governs your coverage, and Sun Life or your plan administrator can confirm what your plan pays.</p>

